Purpose: Explain the Nintendo DS implementation, its causal development
journey and relevant shared systems without repackaging the GBA book.

Tasks:
- [x] Author a source-pinned, chaptered NDS-only manuscript with diagrams,
      algorithms, design principles, worked examples and explained exercises.
- [x] Explain historical failures, compatibility boundaries and parked tests.
- [x] Reuse the locked local book toolchain to create a new searchable PDF
      and self-contained HTML reader without replacing the existing book.
- [x] Inspect native content, links, fonts, clipping and rendered pages.
- [x] Update documentation/navigation without expanding the GIF-first README.
- [ ] Verify preservation, synchronize the issue/Project and publish as Zanark.

Acceptance criteria:
The NDS journey and technical reference have independent paths under
docs/nds-book. No GBA hardware/runtime chapters are included. Shared systems
are explained only where relevant to NDS. The original published GBA PDF
retains SHA256 25875beab7d925f9d014de89842b560216729c799e673f5a7218291aa75db1ad.
No private ROM, recording, transcript or context enters the deliverables.
Source citations use the actual implementation revision. All selected
chapters, diagrams, illustrations, exercises and references appear in the
real PDF/HTML. Report structural, native and bounded visual review separately
from human approval. Keep the existing 21 parked browser cases explicit.

